    "short_description": "A winter weekend getaway at a resort and spa in the White Mountains of New Hampshire with outdoor adventures, spa time and resort activities.",
    "full_description": "Join us for a winter weekend getaway at the Mountain View Grand Resort & Spa in the White Mountains of New Hampshire. This is the first in a new series of Weekend Adventures with Amy and Liz, hosted group trips built around fun destinations, new experiences, and the chance to meet great people without using a whole week of vacation time.\n\nThe weekend runs January 22 to 24, 2027. It is a hosted experience package, and you must book with Amy or Liz. Reach out to either of them for pricing and details.\n\nThere is plenty to look forward to. Head outdoors for scenic winter hikes and snowshoeing through winter landscapes, or take in the mountain scenery and fresh mountain air. When you are ready to slow down, settle in for cozy evenings by the fire, enjoy cocktails, good food, and easy conversation, or book spa treatments and some relaxation time.\n\nThe resort has an indoor pool, sauna, and wellness centre, along with morning yoga to start your day. For something different, try axe throwing and other resort activities, or spend time with movies, games, and plenty of laughs. Resort features include an evening campfire, a movie theatre, a game room, the Harvest Tavern and the Bar at Harvest Tavern, the 1865 Wine Cellar, history tours, the Tower Spa, and Mountain View Farm.\n\nWhether you are looking for outdoor adventures, a relaxing spa weekend, or simply a chance to unwind and have some fun, there is something here for everyone. Everyone is welcome, whether you are a couple, a group of friends, or travelling solo. Come with people you know or come on your own and leave with new friends.\n\nThese shorter getaways are also an easy way to try one of our hosted group trips without committing to a full vacation. If you would like to join, we can help you plan your weekend away. Please note that activities are subject to availability, weather conditions, and change.",
